        "statement": "For each $n\\geq1$, define $\\theta_*:\\F^{2n}\\to\\mathbb R$ by\n\\[\n \\theta_*(x)=\n \\begin{cases}\\pi/2,&x=0\\text{ or }x=\\mathbf1,\\\\0,&\\text{otherwise},\\end{cases}\n \\qquad D_*=\\diag(e^{\\mathrm i\\theta_*(x)}).\n\\]\nThen $\\theta_*(\\bar x)=\\theta_*(x)$. Every allowed circuit with matrix\n$U=cD_*$, for any complex scalar $c$, contains at least\n\\[\n N_m=2^{m-1}+m-2=2^{2n-1}+2n-2\n\\]\nCNOT gates.",
